WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.714
As everyone crowded near the door to the tower, Zann glanced back.

2
00:00:04.715 --> 00:00:09.467
Mouth wide open, the Beast thrust its giant head toward them.

3
00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:10.407
Crash

4
00:00:10.408 --> 00:00:15.059
! The Beast howled with pain and frustration as it hit an invisible

5
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.912
barrier. "I knew it!" Zann exclaimed. "It's a Shield

6
00:00:18.913 --> 00:00:24.093
spell!" "What?" Perda sounded confused. "But we passed straight through

7
00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:29.001
it." "The shield must have been designed to only keep out the Beast," said

8
00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:32.761
Venna. "Nice thinking, boy," Wyssa

9
00:00:32.762 --> 00:00:36.637
added. "But how did you know the shield was there?" Darb asked

10
00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:42.921
Zann. "I figured Morb wouldn't build his lair here if he didn't have a way to keep the Beast out," Zann

11
00:00:42.922 --> 00:00:46.279
explained. "But the mibbit . . ." Perda gestured toward

12
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:55.873
Darb. "I know," Zann said. "I figured, or at least I hoped, that Morb had a backup plan, just in case the mibbit couldn't hold back the

13
00:00:55.874 --> 00:00:58.901
Beast." "That makes sense." Darb stroked the

14
00:00:58.902 --> 00:01:03.778
mibbit. "If I had a monster like that outside my front door, I'd have a backup plan

15
00:01:03.779 --> 00:01:08.401
too!" The Beast let out another howl of fury. Gliss shot it a nervous

16
00:01:08.402 --> 00:01:11.258
look. "What do we do now?" she

17
00:01:11.259 --> 00:01:20.900
asked. "We go in," said Wyssa. "Carefully." Touching the lock on the door, she muttered a few words. The door opened with a

18
00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:25.242
pop. With Wyssa in the lead, the group stepped quietly into the

19
00:01:25.243 --> 00:01:31.525
tower. The entryway inside was long and narrow, lit by a procession of flickering wall

20
00:01:31.526 --> 00:01:39.464
torches. "Weird." Perda peered ahead. "This place looks a lot bigger on the inside than it did from the

21
00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:43.697
outside." "No kidding," Zann said, glancing through an arched

22
00:01:43.698 --> 00:01:48.313
doorway. Beyond was a room so enormous that he couldn't see the far

23
00:01:48.314 --> 00:01:54.162
wall. Gliss was staring through another arch. "How are we going to find Morb in this

24
00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:57.124
place?" "Or my parents." Zann looked at

25
00:01:57.125 --> 00:01:59.851
Wyssa. "Are there any spells we could

26
00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:06.542
use?" "Hundreds," she replied. "But I'm sure Morb has magic sensors in

27
00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:11.312
place. It's better if he doesn't know we're here until we find

28
00:02:11.313 --> 00:02:14.551
him." Suddenly Darb gasped. "Look

29
00:02:14.552 --> 00:02:17.251
out!" Something burst out of a nearby

30
00:02:17.252 --> 00:02:21.630
doorway. "Uh-oh, it's one of those blob monsters," Zann

31
00:02:21.631 --> 00:02:26.015
exclaimed. "Like the one Morb had guarding the palace back in First

32
00:02:26.016 --> 00:02:36.261
City!" "A sweller from Ductilan." Wyssa nodded. "They make crude but effective guards. Fortunately they aren't very

33
00:02:36.262 --> 00:02:43.839
smart." She pulled a handful of stones out of her pocket and tossed them down a side hallway. The sweller blobbed after

34
00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.967
them. "This way," Wyssa said, heading down a different

35
00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:53.163
hall. Zann peered into each room they passed. No two looked the

36
00:02:53.164 --> 00:03:02.260
same. "This place is strange," Perda commented as she and Zann paused in the doorway of a room that appeared to be made entirely out of fish

37
00:03:02.261 --> 00:03:05.856
scales. "Yeah," Zann said. "Just like the guy who built

38
00:03:05.857 --> 00:03:08.168
it." "Look out!" Venna

39
00:03:08.169 --> 00:03:10.842
cried. Several large trolls lumbered toward

40
00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:14.811
them. "Zing, quick!" Darb urged. "Do your thing!"

41
00:03:14.812 --> 00:03:21.087
Whistling his song, Zing flew forward. The trolls stopped, staring at the dragon.

42
00:03:21.088 --> 00:03:27.658
"Hurry! If we get out of sight, they might forget we were ever here." Venna darted around a corner.

43
00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:31.699
By the time the group rounded the next corner, Zing had caught up.

44
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.631
Zann didn't hear any sound of pursuit.

45
00:03:34.632 --> 00:03:38.650
"I think we lost them," he said. "Thanks, little buddy!"

46
00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:44.441
Zing chirped and led the way into a large courtyard filled with trees and shrubs.

47
00:03:44.442 --> 00:03:50.811
"Wow," Perda said. "This place is definitely bigger on the inside than the outside!"

48
00:03:50.812 --> 00:03:57.572
"Perhaps." Wyssa looked worried. "There might be a Bewilderment spell on the whole place.

49
00:03:57.573 --> 00:04:02.805
That would explain why we never pass the same room twice."

50
00:04:02.806 --> 00:04:07.777
"A Bewilderment spell?" Gliss said. "I've never heard of—aah!"

51
00:04:07.778 --> 00:04:11.486
Zann spun around. One of the trees had grabbed Gliss!

52
00:04:11.487 --> 00:04:16.055
"It's a tentacle tree!" Perda cried. "Like in Fardark!"

53
00:04:16.056 --> 00:04:20.733
Wyssa stepped forward. A long, curved knife appeared in her hand.

54
00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:25.026
With one swift movement, she slashed the tentacle in two.

55
00:04:25.027 --> 00:04:29.481
"Get away from it," she ordered. "Hurry!"

56
00:04:29.482 --> 00:04:33.094
The whole group dashed through another door.

57
00:04:33.095 --> 00:04:42.459
"This is awful!" Venna looked petrified. "It's like Morb brought every scary creature from every world to guard this place!"

58
00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:48.443
There was a sudden flurry of wings. Dozens of large birds burst into the room.

59
00:04:48.444 --> 00:04:55.218
"Snuffer geese!" Gliss exclaimed. "Or sniffer geese? I can't tell the difference."

60
00:04:55.219 --> 00:05:00.899
"Doesn't matter," Wyssa said. "Both breeds are nasty when they're annoyed."

61
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.007
Darb took a deep breath. "Honk! Honk!"

62
00:05:05.008 --> 00:05:10.367
"What's your Void friend doing?" Venna hissed at Zann. "He'll only upset them more!"

63
00:05:10.368 --> 00:05:14.672
"Shh!" Zann watched as Darb honked a few more times.

64
00:05:14.673 --> 00:05:20.243
One of the geese honked back. Then the whole flock waddled off!

65
00:05:20.244 --> 00:05:22.687
"Amazing!" Gliss cried.

66
00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:24.336
They all looked at Darb.

67
00:05:24.337 --> 00:05:27.757
He shrugged. "I just told them we didn't mean them any harm.

68
00:05:27.758 --> 00:05:30.372
At least I think that's what I said!"

69
00:05:30.373 --> 00:05:32.354
Venna looked impressed.

70
00:05:32.355 --> 00:05:40.214
"Let's move on," said Wyssa. She led the way into the next room. It was large and dimly lit.

71
00:05:40.215 --> 00:05:46.073
As Zann entered the room, he thought he saw a shadowy shape moving along one wall.

72
00:05:46.074 --> 00:05:49.177
He paused and peered into the dimness.

73
00:05:49.178 --> 00:05:53.507
"Guys?" said Zann. "I think there's something in here."

74
00:05:53.508 --> 00:05:57.164
Just then the shadowy creature stepped into the light.

75
00:05:57.165 --> 00:06:00.494
The creature was orange with black stripes.

76
00:06:00.495 --> 00:06:04.557
Perda gasped. "It's one of those striped monsters.

77
00:06:04.558 --> 00:06:09.874
Like the one Morb sent after that sneaky guy, Slib, back at the palace!"

78
00:06:09.875 --> 00:06:13.349
"How do we fight this creature?" Gliss asked.

79
00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.792
Venna shrugged. "Run!"

80
00:06:15.793 --> 00:06:22.292
Zann was in the lead as they raced around a corner and straight into a flock of tiny, buzzing creatures.

81
00:06:22.293 --> 00:06:27.768
"Flizzes!" he shouted, steeling himself for the little dragons' painful stings.

82
00:06:27.769 --> 00:06:31.563
But it didn't happen. The flizzes immediately buzzed away.

83
00:06:31.564 --> 00:06:36.409
"Wow," Perda said. "We're lucky they didn't attack us."

84
00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:47.811
"Maybe not." Wyssa sounded grim. "They're probably flying straight to Morb to tell him that we're here."

